## What is NOT covered by this licence

Provision *prose* in every corpus is original drafting. Where a provision cites
an external instrument, the citation is a reference and the instrument's own
terms govern that instrument. Each pack's own `LICENSE-DATA` lists the
instruments it references and the terms they carry (US CFR text is a US
Government work in the public domain; EU legal texts are reusable under
Commission Decision 2011/833/EU with the source acknowledged; CWE and CAPEC
identifiers are used under MITRE's royalty-free terms; LOINC codes are subject
to the LOINC licence; PCI DSS, SNOMED CT, AAHA Diagnostic Terms, VeNom, the
ASAP standard, ISO/IEC 42001 and CIS Benchmarks are not redistributed in any
form and are paraphrased in original words where an obligation is expressed).

Nothing in the data is a record of a real organisation, product, person or
decision. The regulators, statutes and standards named are real; every case,
change, provision and enterprise is fictitious.
